# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# Explicit binary declarations for the asset types actually bundled/tracked
# in this repo (fonts, hall/outcome icons, screenshots, sample exports) -
# not strictly required (Git's own content-sniffing already classifies these
# correctly today), but pins that classification instead of depending on the
# heuristic succeeding, and documents intent for anyone editing this file.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.xlsx binary
*.db binary

# Shell scripts must always check out with LF, even on a Windows client with
# core.autocrlf=true - a CRLF line ending in a script's shebang/body breaks
# execution under bash/WSL/CI ("bad interpreter" / "$'\r': command not
# found"). No .sh files are tracked today, but this is cheap insurance
# against that classic Windows-Git gotcha if one ever is.
*.sh text eol=lf
